    "Read-only shell commands in the built-in allowlist (cat, head, tail, ls, find without -delete/-exec, git diff/log/status/show, rg, grep, wc, file, stat, which, pwd, echo, …) run without asking. Commands outside the allowlist are passed to a one-shot LLM judge running on the active provider's **Flash** model (cheap & fast — never Pro), and only YES verdicts auto-run. Destructive patterns (rm, sudo, git push --force, git reset --hard, …) still require typing \"confirm\"." : {

